  "description": "From July 2026, as part of the preparation for redetermination of the Holocaust Memorial and Learning Centre planning application, updated documents from the applicant, including updates to the Environmental Statement, are being made publicly available on the Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government website: \rhttps://www.gov.uk/guidance/holocaust-memorial-and-learning-centre-updated-planning-application-documents \r,alongside details of how to make representations on the available information.\r\rDetails of the Holocaust Memorial Act 2026 and the Bill's passage to Royal Assent can be found:\rhttps://bills.parliament.uk/bills/3421\rhttps://www.gov.uk/government/publications/holocaust-memorial-bill-government-response-to-the-house-of-lords-select-committee-report/holocaust-memorial-bill-government-response-to-the-house-of-lords-select-committee-report\r\rOn 8 April 2022, the High Court quashed the decision by the Minister of State for Housing to grant planning permission for the installation of the UK Holocaust Memorial and Learning Centre at Victoria Tower Gardens.\r\rApplication called by the Minister of State for Housing (ref: APP/XF990/V/19/3240661) for:\rInstallation of the United Kingdom Holocaust Memorial and Learning Centre including excavation to provide a basement and basement mezzanine for the learning centre (Class D1); erection of a single storey entrance pavilion; re-provision of the Horseferry Playground and refreshments kiosk (Class A1); repositioning of the Spicer Memorial; new hard and soft landscaping and lighting around the site; and all ancillary and associated works.",
